error[E0277]: `std::string::String` is not ordered: the ordering operators are answered over the integer types only
  --> tests/ui/op_order_on_text.rs:13:44
   |
13 |     let _ = cipher.query(op::Lt, "nguyen").on(&name_plan);
   |                                            ^^ no ordering operator over this type
   |
   = help: the trait `Ordered` is not implemented for `std::string::String`
   = note: `Lt`, `Lte`, `Gt`, `Gte` and `Between` take `u8` to `u128` or `i8` to `i128`; the order of text is not settled (ADR-0009), so an ordering over text does not compile
   = help: the following other types implement trait `Ordered`:
             i128
             i16
             i32
             i64
             i8
             u128
             u16
             u32
           and $N others
   = note: required for `stack_encrypt::op::Lt` to implement `DefaultIndex<std::string::String>`
   = note: required for `ValuePlan<std::string::String, Indexed<stack_encrypt::Ore>>` to implement `Chooses<stack_encrypt::op::Lt, std::string::String, Whole>`
